{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123000","id":4395900322,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBgQdog","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123000","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123000.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123000.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123000","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123000/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123000/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123000/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d0b655faea05608672dd9d2aa2b272e092818b39","number":123000,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix infinite layout loop caused by `desired_size` circular dependency","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This prevents a circular dependency between a child's desired size and its parent's dynamic maximum-size cache during layout.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122944\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nFixes an infinite layout loop that can freeze the editor when using an autowrapped `Label` inside a `BoxContainer`.\r\n\r\nThe issue comes from a circular dependency during layout. `BoxContainer` uses `get_bound_desired_size()` when calculating the space for its children, and then updates the child's `parent_maximum_size_cache`. That cache is also used when calculating the child's combined maximum size.\r\n\r\nFor an autowrapped `Label`, its desired size can depend on the width available to it. This means the parent can change the child's maximum size, which changes the label's desired size, which then changes the size calculated by the parent again. In some configurations this repeats indefinitely.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes the relevant desired-size calculations so they don't use the parent's dynamic maximum-size cache when applying the control's own maximum-size constraints. **It does this by calculating a \"local maximum\" that still fully respects `get_maximum_size()` and `custom_maximum_size`, ensuring user-defined limits are preserved.**\r\n\r\n## Before:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad758af0-82cb-48f2-ab56-12bfc355734a\r\n\r\n## After:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b527105d-f4e4-4f59-8842-d221ad1b0bac","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"",